worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_meta_synthesis.js"
  ceiling 645
  rationale "Synthesis half of the meta reasoner (2026-10-06 meta-algorithm doctrine): typed program enumeration over the seeded instruction set, parameter and threshold inference from the request's examples, rendering, and verification of the exact source the answer shows. Split from formal_ai_worker_meta_reasoner.js to stay under the 1000-line file limit. Ceiling moved 472 to 520 for rewrite-head fitting, measure parts covering their words, and the tied-word and plural-view tie-breaks. Ceiling moved 520 to 620 for binding the values a request names by type and order, text-measure filters (containment), selectors over a measure (maximum_by), and rendering text parameters as literals. Ceiling moved 620 to 645 for enumerating only the programs that use the head operation (metaStepUsesAny and the mustUse bound of metaPrograms): the synthesis kept just those, but built all 4.8 million length-three list_text programs per pass first, so a plain shell request (run ls command) spent 16 seconds in the solver and the issue-1021 suite outran its CI shard budget; it now takes about 4 seconds with the same answers."
